{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The retained-store checks prove useful parts of the correspondence, but they do not yet make reconstruction self-contained: replay still calls the checkout’s compiler. A recording-only contract would drop the source-to-compiled-tree check. I’m working toward an addressed reconstruction package with an explicit runtime boundary, so the requirement is neither “trust a commit” nor “archive the entire machine.”"}}
