{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1720,1765p;1825,1850p'; nl -ba test/yang/clojure_test.clj | sed -n '2460,2525p'; nl -ba test/yang/correspondence_lane.clj | sed -n '1,130p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1720\t\n  1721\t\n  1722\t(defn expand-batch\n  1723\t  \"Expand one input batch against `ctx` (§3.2). Returns\n  1724\t   `{:status :ok :tree packet :log log :ctx ctx'}` or\n  1725\t   `{:status :error :error e :log log :ctx ctx'}`. Either way `ctx'` has\n  1726\t   consumed the batch (`:t` + 1) and every attempt it allocated; only\n  1727\t   success changes the store, to the post-harvest store. A success also\n  1728\t   carries `:frontend-metadata` — the C1 side table finalized over the\n  1729\t   final tree (`final-call-site-metadata`), covering the tree that\n  1730\t   actually executes — when, and only when, the selected member itself\n  1731\t   claimed C1 coverage (its own verdict in `batch-call-site-claims`); a\n  1732\t   sibling's claim never manufactures a table for it, and an unclaimed\n  1733\t   batch carries no table at all, never an empty one. The admission\n  1734\t   this expansion produced the tree under rides beside it as\n  1735\t   `:call-site-origin` — the source origin of the admitted run member,\n  1736\t   the key the table is stored and resolved under beside the final\n  1737\t   root address. It is the table's admission key, not a blanket\n  1738\t   stamp: each row's origin is that occurrence's own (§2.1, §2.3) —\n  1739\t   a retained occurrence keeps its own incoming provenance (its\n  1740\t   source origin, or the generating expansion's, however deeply it\n  1741\t   was passed through), and generated syntax carries the\n  1742\t   `[:expansion record-address]` of the recorded expansion event\n  1743\t   whose output introduced it. A context\n  1744\t   store binding a\n  1745\t   reserved name, or holding an entry without the current AST contract,\n  1746\t   is refused (Rule R): it is a composition defect, so it throws rather\n  1747\t   than returning an error.\"\n  1748\t  [batch ctx]\n  1749\t  (check-store! (:store ctx))\n  1750\t  (let [ctx (with-default-guards ctx)\n  1751\t        source-batch (:t ctx)\n  1752\t        base {:ctx ctx, :source-batch source-batch, :events [], :produced []}\n  1753\t        finish (fn [st]\n  1754\t                 (let [ctx' (update (:ctx st) :t inc)]\n  1755\t                   (if-let [e (:error st)]\n  1756\t                     {:status :error, :error e, :log (log-packet st), :ctx ctx'}\n  1757\t                     {:status :ok, :tree (:tree st), :log (log-packet st),\n  1758\t                      :frontend-metadata (:frontend-metadata st),\n  1759\t                      :call-site-origin (:call-site-origin st),\n  1760\t                      :ctx (assoc ctx' :store (:next-store st))})))\n  1761\t        {:keys [admitted error]} (admit batch)]\n  1762\t    (if error\n  1763\t      (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt base)]\n  1764\t        (finish (-> st\n  1765\t                    (record-event (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter) source-batch\n  1825\t                    ;; the selected member's own verdict decides its\n  1826\t                    ;; metadata; a sibling's claim never manufactures a\n  1827\t                    ;; table for a member that made none\n  1828\t                    claims (batch-call-site-claims batch)\n  1829\t                     metadata (when (and claims (nth claims run-index))\n  1830\t                                (final-call-site-metadata\n  1831\t                                  (packet->row-set tree)\n  1832\t                                  (:call-site-origins st) origin))]\n  1833\t                (if-let [e (valid-tree? tree)]\n  1834\t                  (throw (ex-info \"Expander produced a non-canonical tree\" e))\n  1835\t                  (finish (assoc st :tree tree :next-store next-store\n  1836\t                                 :frontend-metadata metadata\n  1837\t                                  :call-site-origin (when metadata origin))))))))))))\n  1838\t\n  1839\t\n  1840\t(defn expand\n  1841\t  \"`expand-batch` returning the tree packet, or throwing `ex-info` carrying\n  1842\t   the error data.\"\n  1843\t  [batch ctx]\n  1844\t  (let [{:keys [status tree error]} (expand-batch batch ctx)]\n  1845\t    (if (= :ok status)\n  1846\t      tree\n  1847\t      (throw (ex-info \"Macro expansion failed\" error)))))\n  1848\t\n  1849\t\n  1850\t(defn make-ctx\n  2460\t   `cell/authentic?` once a callee passes the cell-ref shape pre-filter,\n  2461\t   and a spliced `cell/new` mints genuine references (the engine seals\n  2462\t   them under the test composition's capability secret), so the lane's\n  2463\t   registry supplies the cell host as the linked compositions' do.\"\n  2464\t  (let [host (fn [registry module-name fns arities]\n  2465\t               (module/register-host-module\n  2466\t                 registry module-name fns\n  2467\t                 (into {} (map (fn [[op _]]\n  2468\t                                 [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\n  2469\t                       fns)))\n  2470\t        portable (into {}\n  2471\t                       (map (fn [[source _]]\n  2472\t                              (let [op (symbol (name source))]\n  2473\t                                [op (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message\n  2474\t                                                          (get data/data-module op))])))\n  2475\t                       yang/library-adapters)]\n  2476\t    (-> av-modules\n  2477\t        (module/register-cell-module)\n  2478\t        (host 'kind yang/kind-module yang/kind-arities)\n  2479\t        (host 'portable portable\n  2480\t              (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\n  2481\t                    (keys portable))))))\n  2482\t\n  2483\t\n  2484\t(def ^:private library-opts\n  2485\t  {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true\n  2486\t   :adapters yang/library-adapters\n  2487\t   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\n  2488\t\n  2489\t\n  2490\t(defn run-guest-machine\n  2491\t  \"Run an AST through either observer composition with a finite instruction\n  2492\t   budget. Return the terminal machine so fixtures can observe its streams.\"\n  2493\t  [ast modules lane step-limit]\n  2494\t  (let [run-bounded (fn [machine]\n  2495\t                      (loop [v machine, n 0]\n  2496\t                        (cond\n  2497\t                          (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n  2498\t                          (= n step-limit) (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n  2499\t                                                           {:lane lane :steps n :consumer v}))\n  2500\t                          :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n)))))\n  2501\t        semantic? (= lane :semantic)\n  2502\t        machine (if semantic?\n  2503\t                  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n  2504\t                                       :capability-secret tu/secret :modules modules})\n  2505\t                  (tu/create-vm {:modules modules}))\n  2506\t        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)\n  2507\t        load-program (if semantic?\n  2508\t                       (fn [v rows stamp]\n  2509\t                         (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n  2510\t                         (semantic/load-vector v (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n  2511\t                                               vm/semantic-contract))\n  2512\t                       ast-walker/vm-load-program)\n  2513\t        queued ((if semantic? tu/queue-rows! tu/queue-ast!) session ast)]\n  2514\t    (-> (observer/run-on-stream queued engine/ready-for-ingress?\n  2515\t                                (vm/fresh-code-loader load-program vm/ast-contract)\n  2516\t                                run-bounded)\n  2517\t        :consumer)))\n  2518\t\n  2519\t\n  2520\t(defn run-guest-machine-depth\n  2521\t  \"Like run-guest-machine, but records the maximum continuation depth\n  2522\t   (the semantic lane's K-vector length, or the walker lane's :next chain\n  2523\t   length) across the run, and returns the terminal machine with the max\n  2524\t   depth attached under `:max-depth`.\"\n  2525\t  [ast modules lane step-limit]\n     1\t(ns yang.correspondence-lane\n     2\t  \"Measurement-only JVM composition for the D1 C lanes. Not a verifier.\"\n     3\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n     4\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n     5\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n     6\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as walker]\n     7\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n     8\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n     9\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n    10\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t(defn run-measured!\n    14\t  \"Run the observer composition with one aggregate step budget. Answers the\n    15\t   terminal machine and exact number of vm/step calls, including across\n    16\t   multiple observer run callbacks. A blocked machine is not a completed lane.\"\n    17\t  [ast modules lane step-limit & [{:keys [check!]}]]\n    18\t  (when-not (and (contains? #{:walker :semantic} lane) (nat-int? step-limit)\n    19\t                 (or (nil? check!) (ifn? check!)))\n    20\t    (throw (ex-info \"Invalid lane or budget\" {:stage :configuration})))\n    21\t  (let [steps (atom 0)\n    22\t        run (fn [machine]\n    23\t              (loop [v machine]\n    24\t                (when check! (check! @steps v))\n    25\t                (cond\n    26\t                  (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n    27\t                  (= @steps step-limit)\n    28\t                  (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n    29\t                                  {:stage :instruction-limit :lane lane\n    30\t                                   :steps @steps :consumer v}))\n    31\t                  :else (let [v' (vm/step v)]\n    32\t                          (swap! steps inc)\n    33\t                          (recur v')))))\n    34\t        semantic? (= lane :semantic)\n    35\t        machine (if semantic?\n    36\t                  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n    37\t                                       :capability-secret tu/secret :modules modules})\n    38\t                  (tu/create-vm {:modules modules}))\n    39\t        load-program (if semantic?\n    40\t                       (fn [v rows stamp]\n    41\t                         (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n    42\t                         (semantic/load-vector v (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n    43\t                                               vm/semantic-contract))\n    44\t                       walker/vm-load-program)\n    45\t        session ((if semantic? tu/queue-rows! tu/queue-ast!)\n    46\t                 (tu/make-observer-session machine) ast)\n    47\t        answer (observer/run-on-stream session engine/ready-for-ingress?\n    48\t                                       (vm/fresh-code-loader load-program vm/ast-contract)\n    49\t                                       run)]\n    50\t    (when-not (zero? (get-in answer [:observer :ingress-gaps]))\n    51\t      (throw (ex-info \"Program stream gap\" {:stage :ingress-gap})))\n    52\t    {:machine (:consumer answer) :steps @steps}))\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\t(defn read-trace!\n    56\t  \"Read a halted lane's ring trace, refusing any evicted prefix or incomplete\n    57\t   drain. Byte size is UTF-8 pr-str of the vector, not in-memory occupancy.\"\n    58\t  [handle]\n    59\t  (let [old (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)\n    60\t        new (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-newest)\n    61\t        start (:dao.stream/cursor old)\n    62\t        end (:dao.stream/cursor new)\n    63\t        first-position (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/position start)\n    64\t        tail (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/position end)]\n    65\t    (when-not (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome old))\n    66\t                   (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome new))\n    67\t                   (integer? first-position) (integer? tail)\n    68\t                   (= (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity start)\n    69\t                      (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity end)))\n    70\t      (throw (ex-info \"Unrecognized trace cursor\" {:stage :trace-cursor})))\n    71\t    (when-not (zero? first-position)\n    72\t      (throw (ex-info \"Trace prefix evicted\" {:stage :trace-loss :lost first-position})))\n    73\t    (loop [cursor start, records []]\n    74\t      (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n    75\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n    76\t          :dao.stream/ok (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n    77\t                                (conj records (:dao.stream/value result)))\n    78\t          (:dao.stream/blocked :dao.stream/end)\n    79\t          (if (and (= cursor end) (= tail (count records)))\n    80\t            {:records records :record-count (count records)\n    81\t             :serialized-bytes (alength (.getBytes (pr-str records) \"UTF-8\"))\n    82\t             :max-record-bytes (reduce max 0 (map #(alength (.getBytes (pr-str %) \"UTF-8\")) records))\n    83\t             :lost 0 :drain-outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)}\n    84\t            (throw (ex-info \"Incomplete trace drain\" {:stage :trace-drain})))\n    85\t          (throw (ex-info \"Trace read refused\" {:stage :trace-drain\n    86\t                                                :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)})))))))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn trace-reachable-heap!\n    90\t  \"Measure the trace handle's reachable heap using a supplied host sizer.\n    91\t